3. **PHASE SCOPE.** No integration with HP tools; if a ticket needs one, STOP and ask Tuesday.
4. **No production, no demo deploy, no hosted site, no HTTP to any hosted host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no App Service setting.** The only network is `npm ci`, a missing-browser `npx playwright install chromium`, `git push`/`git fetch`, `gh` and Jira GETs, plus your own loopback servers in 9850-9859 (stop every one you start; record the ports free again).
5. **No message to any human.** No mail, chat or PR comment; you never open, merge, edit or comment on a PR and never write Jira. No person's name in STATUS, code, test titles or commit messages (say "the product owner"). Client names: Datasec/HPSM-POC only. No Artifact, Docs, publish, decision-queue or scoreboard tool. You never copy the design file into the repository.
6. **WORDS.** See THE SHAPE item 4 and D-5. Customer-facing words are the product owner's: you add no new visible string; any word a ticket or the design seems to need that the app does not already show is a question for Tuesday in STATUS (FOR TUESDAY), never a guess. Print a changed-string table for Tuesday (expected: empty).
7. **Never skip a failure.** Fix the root cause and re-verify end to end; never `skip`, `only`, retry, sleep-for-timing or environment-gate. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`); quarantine to `.tools/b956/_quarantine/`. A mutant file is restored by `cp` from the committed blob.
8. **Shell:** never type `cd` (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); `git -C`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; write `${VAR}:path`, never `$VAR:path`; heredocs QUOTED (`<<'EOF'`); python only as `python3 -I -B`; never an unquoted word starting with `=`. **Every count printed in STATUS is printed by the command that makes it.** Stop every process you start; kill only by pid plus proven cwd. Never wait with `pgrep -f <pattern>` from a shell whose own argv holds the pattern.
